When an extension’s registered content scripts change, Ladybird sends
the page processes that extension’s registered scripts alone. Firefox
does the same: ExtensionUserScripts broadcasts just the scripts
involved, in an Extension:RegisterContentScripts message or its Update
or Unregister counterpart, and ExtensionProcessScript applies them to
that extension’s WebExtensionPolicy in each content process. Chromium’s
UserScriptLoader::SendUpdate() sends a renderer UpdateUserScripts() with
the scripts of one owner, named by that owner’s HostID. And WebKit’s
WebExtensionContext::scriptingRegisterContentScripts() adds just the new
scripts, through addInjectedContent().
